 "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15440, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CmrBQrK7abQwGfAiscwexn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18166, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Joc9zgfi24tzdajCgJhdV1", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 health failures before redeploying; investigate the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 48766, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Joc9zgfi24tzdajCgJhdV1", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 48766, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Joc9zgfi24tzdajCgJhdV1", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 50031, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01BX7amu3JGu196m8WmeNhF9", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 50331, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BX7amu3JGu196m8WmeNhF9", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 50331, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BX7amu3JGu196m8WmeNhF9", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 52518, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again. Error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has a healthy production record.\n- **Incident:** The create call timed out, but the incident was recorded. I checked the incident list and found it as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I did not retry, so the on-call engineer was paged only once. The description covers the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nFollow-ups are noted in the incident: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health failures before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator partial failure from the first rollback attempt.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_012FDUGV77PXJRggFBra6yKR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WtikWm9KxBSsNnmyKDKcCm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "in