ions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down from 0.18 to 0.002. Next I'll open the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Joc9zgfi24tzdajCgJhdV1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18 across us-east, us-west, eu-west). Action taken: rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 and v2.3.0 were healthy; v2.3.1 unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error), leaving the service mixed (us-east v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate root cause of v2.3.1 health failures before redeploying; investigate the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.0-sev2-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. Before retrying, I'll check whether it was created, so the on-call engineer isn't paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BX7amu3JGu196m8WmeNhF9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions and healthy again. Error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, and it completed in us-east, us-west and eu-west. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 has a healthy production record.\n- **Incident:** The create call timed out, but the incident was recorded. I checked the incident list and found it as **INC-0001** (SEV2, checkout-api, open). I did not retry, so the on-call engineer was paged only once. The description covers the rollback, the partial failure and the retry.\n\nFollow-ups are noted in the incident: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 health failures before redeploying, and look into the orchestrator partial failure from the first rollback attempt.", "type": "text"}]}]}